{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 18, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a member of the House of Toulouse and the last ruler of the County of Tripoli. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. Raymond III was born around 1152 and succeeded his father as the Count of Tripoli in 1152. He was a vassal of the Kingdom of Jerusalem.\n\n*Early Life and Reign* \nRaymond III was a minor when he succeeded his father and as such the regency was given to his mother Hodierna of Jerusalem. She held this position until 1160. Raymond III's early reign was marked by conflicts with the Kingdom of Armenia. In 1163 he allied with the Kingdom of Jerusalem to fight against the Kingdom of Armenia. This alliance led to the Battle of Artah in 1163 where Raymond III was captured by the Armenian forces. \n\n*Reign and Campaigns* \nRaymond III was held captive by the Armenian forces for several years. During this time he was released and he made a truce with the Armenian king. However this truce was short lived and Raymond III resumed hostilities against the Armenian forces. He also fought against the forces of the Fatimid Caliphate of Egypt. He also launched a campaign against the County of Edessa in 1173. Raymond III died in 1187 after being wounded in a battle against the forces of Saladin the Ayyubid Sultan of Egypt.\n\n*Succession and Legacy* \nRaymond III was succeeded by his daughter Isabella of Tripoli who was married to Bohemond IV Prince of Antioch. She died in 1201 without any children. The County of Tripoli was then inherited by the Prince of Antioch.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.014390614}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -0.00016938205}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0010648064}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.1300828}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.349725e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.00021371941}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -6.651657e-05}, {